.TH MWIN 1 "September 2026" "mwin 0.3.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mwin \- minimal fullscreen terminal window manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mwin
.RB [ \-c " key" ]
.RB [ \-s ]
.RI [ command " [" argument " ...]]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mwin
runs multiple independent pseudo-terminals in one terminal and displays one
at a time. It provides fullscreen windows and per-window scrollback, but no
split panes or session server. Run it under
.BR abduco (1)
for persistent attach/detach sessions. Run
.BR mtm (1)
as an ordinary command inside a window when split panes are needed.
.PP
One row is reserved for a window list unless disabled with
.BR \-s .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-c " key"
Set the command prefix. The argument may be a literal character, caret notation
such as
.BR ^G ,
or a decimal byte value.
.TP
.B \-s
Hide the status line and give every row to the child terminal.
.TP
.BR \-h , " --help"
Print usage and exit.
.TP
.B \-v
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B --self-test
Run internal VT and scrollback tests and exit.
.SH WINDOW KEYS
Commands use
.B Ctrl-o
by default.
.TP
.B m
Create a shell window.
.TP
.B o
Return to the previously visited window. Repeated commands toggle between the
two most recently visited windows.
.TP
.BR Ctrl-n , " Ctrl-p"
Select the next or previous window.
.TP
.BR 1\-9 , " 0"
Select window 1 through 10.
.TP
.B Ctrl-x
Send SIGHUP to the current window's process group and close it.
.TP
.B Ctrl-l
Redraw the screen.
.TP
.B Ctrl-u
Enter scrollback and move one page backward.
.TP
.B ?
Display the key summary until another key is pressed.
.TP
.B Ctrl-o
When entered after the prefix, send a literal Ctrl-o to the application.
.PP
After the prefix is entered, the status line indicates that mwin is waiting for
a command key. The configured prefix is displayed. No indication is shown when
the status line is disabled with
.BR \-s .
.SH SCROLLBACK KEYS
Once scrollback is active, the following keys need no prefix:
.TP
.B Ctrl-u
Move one page backward.
.TP
.B Ctrl-d
Move one page forward.
.TP
.B k
Move one row upward toward older output.
.TP
.B j
Move one row downward toward newer output.
.TP
.B g
Move to the oldest retained row.
.TP
.B G
Return to the live terminal.
.TP
.B Escape
Leave scrollback and return to the live terminal.
.PP
Incoming output continues to be processed while scrollback is visible. Only
rows scrolled off the primary screen are retained; alternate-screen activity
is excluded. Soft-wrapped primary-screen and historical lines are reflowed
after a resize; hard newlines remain separate. Rows displaced by a height
reduction enter scrollback. Reflowed rows count toward the configured history
limit; when MWIN_SCROLLBACK is 0, content outside the live screen is discarded.
.PP
Soft-wrapped rows are reproduced as terminal autowraps on the hosting terminal.
Selecting them with the hosting terminal's copy command therefore does not
insert a newline that was absent from the original output.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SHELL
Shell used for new windows. The user's login shell and /bin/sh are fallbacks.
.TP
.B MWIN_SCROLLBACK
Maximum number of scrollback rows retained independently for each window.
The default is 2000. A value of 0 disables scrollback.
.TP
.B TERM
Describes the hosting terminal. Child terminals receive screen-256color by
default; this is configurable in config.h.
.TP
.B MWIN
Set to 1 in child processes.
.SH PERSISTENCE
For a persistent workspace, use:
.PP
.RS
.B abduco -A main mwin
.RE
.PP
The default abduco detach key is Ctrl-backslash. Mwin keeps child PTYs drained
while detached and redraws on terminal resize or with its redraw key.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Mwin has no search, copy mode, split layout, or plugin system. OSC clipboard
and hyperlink sequences and graphical terminal protocols are not passed
through.
.PP
Mwin forwards a standalone Escape immediately. A nested ncurses program such
as mtm may apply its own Escape delay; for mtm this can be shortened, for
example, with
.BR "ESCDELAY=25 mtm" .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR abduco (1),
.BR mtm (1),
.BR pty (7)
